Id: perm019w
Severity: WARN
Category: filesystem
Check: check_perms

The /etc directory is not owned by root, or its group is not the
expected one. Almost every security decision on the system lives in a
file under /etc, so the wrong owner there can rewrite passwords,
sudoers, SSH keys and service definitions. Restore it with
chown root:root /etc, and check for files under it that changed hands
at the same time. (The ALERT-era entry perm019a above is kept so old
reports still explain.)
